  "narrative": "All twelve new discovery analyses have valid Welch cells and are interpreted on the signed scale already aligned to each registered direction. A positive signed estimate supports the claimed direction, and the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold is applied to the signed lower bound. The central result is that feature_010 shows threshold-exceeding effect modification by feature_038 and feature_018 tails even when the low tail of the other standardized assay is excluded. H110 tests the high feature_038 attenuation interaction among participants with feature_018 at least -1: signed estimate +0.704, 95% CI +0.431 to +0.977. The lower bound is far above threshold, so the discovery evidence supports a dataset-internal attenuation of the feature_010 higher-outcome association in the high feature_038 tail. I accept H110 as a discovery claim and keep it active because it is central to the unresolved H100 pattern and because the unrestricted high-feature_038 interaction failed independent threshold reproduction; I request independent validation. H111 tests the analogous high feature_018 attenuation interaction among feature_038 at least -1: signed +0.921, CI +0.629 to +1.214, so I accept it and keep the investigation active as a possible later validation target. These two sensitivity interactions make the earlier tail pattern more than contamination by the opposite assay low tail, but they remain unadjusted and correlated-assay subgroup contrasts, not pure single-assay modifications or causal claims. H112 and H113 test high-tail feature_010 mean differences in the claimed higher-outcome direction after excluding the opposite assay low tail. H112 is not supported: signed -0.222, CI -0.470 to +0.027; reject and close. H113 is also not supported in the claimed direction: signed -0.435, CI -0.707 to -0.164; reject and close. The H113 raw interval is entirely in the opposite direction, suggesting a possible reversal in the high feature_018 tail after excluding low feature_038, so I registered a separate reversal proposal linked to H113 rather than accepting that opposite-direction claim on this card. H114 and H115 directly test feature_036 interactions for feature_010: H114 signed +0.038, CI -0.254 to +0.330; H115 signed +0.119, CI -0.135 to +0.373. Both fail threshold, so feature_036 does not appear to modify the feature_010 association at the tested cutoff, localizing the observed heterogeneity mainly to feature_038 and feature_018 while preserving the accepted feature_036 tail mean associations. H35 and H36 confirm feature_037 remains strongly associated with lower outcome_001/stronger dependency in both feature_036 tails: +0.810, CI +0.688 to +0.931 and +0.870, CI +0.753 to +0.987; both accepted and closed. H106 and H107 confirm feature_002 remains strongly associated with higher outcome_001/weaker dependency in feature_036 tails: +0.830, CI +0.663 to +0.998 and +0.766, CI +0.592 to +0.940; both accepted and closed. Broad categorical screens H67 and H68 do not reach the scientific threshold: H67 signed +0.074, CI +0.010 to +0.138, and H68 signed -0.029, CI -0.114 to +0.056; both rejected and closed. Overall, the three central axes remain robust, feature_036 does not add interaction evidence for feature_010, and feature_038/feature_018 tail interactions are now supported at discovery threshold but should be treated as internal associations pending validation and careful multiplicity-aware interpretation.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 appraise update. New discovery results support feature_010 assay-tail effect modification. H110 high feature_038 attenuation among feature_018 >= -1: R91 +0.704 CI +0.431 to +0.977, accepted at discovery threshold but active because it refines unresolved H100; validate H110. H111 high feature_018 attenuation among feature_038 >= -1: R92 +0.921 CI +0.629 to +1.214, accepted active and possible future validation target. H112 high feature_038 mean fails claimed higher-outcome direction R93 -0.222 CI -0.470 to +0.027. H113 high feature_018 mean fails claimed direction R94 -0.435 CI -0.707 to -0.164 but suggests possible reversal; registered reversal proposal direction -1 parent H113. H114/H115 feature_036 interactions for feature_010 fail threshold, so feature_036 heterogeneity is limited; accepted feature_036 tail means remain. H35/H36 feature_037 robust in feature_036 tails, accepted closed. H106/H107 feature_002 robust in feature_036 tails, accepted closed. H67/H68 categorical contrasts below threshold, rejected closed. Plan: assess H110 validation in synthesis before strengthening exact feature_038 attenuation. If H110 validation passes threshold, accept H110 more robustly and consider validating H111 if budget remains. If H110 fails, delimit exact high feature_038 attenuation, preserve accepted overall feature_010 main effect, low feature_038 mean/interaction, and feature_018 interactions as dataset-internal discoveries unless later reassessed. Avoid interpreting feature_038/feature_018 interactions as pure single-assay modifications because these standardized assays are unadjusted and may be correlated; also avoid post-hoc reversal claims unless separately registered and analyzed. All conclusions remain dataset-internal associations, not causal, mechanistic, or generalizable.",
